Not useless.  Not stunningly useful, and you could probably easily ascend
without casting spells.  But any late-game combat character with DSM, a robe,
and 18/18 Int/Wis (or more with brilliance) can probably cast some spells.
Even a 50% chance of identify can be useful.  light and charm monster can be
useful, magic mapping is very good if you can do it and if you can you can
also do detect treasure, which is also useful in Gehennom if you're still
looking for such.  And there's cause fear.  Force bolt is nice for blasting
boulders without hauling out a pick-axe.

You don't have the power to cast a lot, of course, but you can still get some
use out of it all.

Knights make a much bigger jump, from "dumb and encased in metal" to "lots of
power, guaranteed Quest robe, and big damage bonus."

